    "23391": {
        "order_id": 8,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "Sequences and Series",
        "question_type": "Practical",
        "exam_year": "2010",
        "question_text": "<p>Find the sum of the first $10$ terms of the arithmetic sequence $2, 5, 8, \\ldots$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The first term $a = 2$ and common difference $d = 3$. The sum of the first $n$ terms is given by $S_n = \\frac{n}{2} [2a + (n-1)d]$. For $n = 10$, $S_{10} = \\frac{10}{2} [2(2) + 9(3)] = 5 [4 + 27] = 5 \\times 31 = 155$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [],
